From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:35:32 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Connect writes the config files itself, so an
 editor extension alone connects

Someone with only VS Code and its GitHub Copilot or Codex extension, and no
`code`, `codex` or `copilot` on the PATH, couldn't connect: Connect ran
`code --add-mcp` and `codex mcp add`. Connect now writes the files those
tools read (merged with what's there, the first old file kept as
.meridian-backup), and the rows read the same files back:

- VS Code (Copilot's agent mode): "servers" of the profile's mcp.json
  (~/Library/Application Support/Code/User, %APPDATA%\Code\User,
  ~/.config/Code/User). Found by the app, `code`, its profile folder or
  the Copilot extension in ~/.vscode/extensions.
- Codex (CLI, VS Code extension, app): [mcp_servers.meridian] in
  config.toml of CODEX_HOME / each Codex account; only that table is
  written or taken out. Found by the extension as "Codex (VS Code
  extension)", or by the app.
- GitHub Copilot: "mcpServers" of $COPILOT_HOME/mcp-config.json, else
  ~/.copilot.
- Visual Studio 2022 17.14+ (Windows): "servers" of %USERPROFILE%\.mcp.json.

A row found only through an extension or an app says so, and that Ask and
Improve with AI need Claude Code, with an Install button.

